   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/DEU.34.1#p1-a84726bc",
     "text": "Which was a part of mount Abarim, Nu 27:12.",
     "label": "a",
     "anchor": "Nebo",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "Nu 27:12",
       "ref": "NUM.27.12"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "geneva/DEU.34.2",
   "range": "DEU.34.2",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "4bc36013",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/DEU.34.2#p1-4bc36013",
     "text": "Called Mediterranean.",
     "label": "b",
     "anchor": "sea"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "geneva/DEU.34.6",
   "range": "DEU.34.6",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "1e1b97fb",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/DEU.34.6#p1-5c7bb228",
     "text": "That is, the angel of the Lord, Jude 1:9.",
     "label": "c",
     "anchor": "he buried him in a valley",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "Jude 1:9",
       "ref": "JUD.1.9"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "geneva/DEU.34.6#p2-123a1c9a",
     "text": "That the Jews might not have opportunity to commit idolatry by it.",
     "label": "d",
     "anchor": "this day"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "geneva/DEU.34.9",
   "range": "DEU.34.9",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "826b8dda",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/DEU.34.9#p1-826b8dda",
     "text": "By this the favour of God is demonstrated, in that he does not leave his Church destitute of a governor.",
     "label": "e",
     "anchor": "Joshua the son of Nun was"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "geneva/DEU.34.10",
   "range": "DEU.34.10",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "7452f076",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/DEU.34.10#p1-7452f076",
     "text": "To whom the Lord revealed himself so plainly as in Ex 33:11.",
     "label": "f",
     "anchor": "face to face",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "Ex 33:11",
       "ref": "EXO.33.11"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "geneva/DEU.34.12",
   "range": "DEU.34.12",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "5c8660bd",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/DEU.34.12#p1-5c8660bd",
     "text": "Meaning, the power of God working by Moses in the wilderness.",
     "label": "g",
     "anchor": "hand"
    }
   ]
  }
 ]
}
